{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Elohim spoke to Moses</b> — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 6:2): He spoke with him in a chastening manner, because he had been harsh in saying and speaking, \"Why have you done evil to this people?\" (above 5:22). <b>And He said to him, I am HaShem</b> — trustworthy to pay the reward of those who walk before Me in integrity. And in this expression we find that it is expounded in several places, etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:16:13.391317729Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}